description:
The "All nodes" checkbox in the ingester settings UI is UI sugar over a frozen `repeated bytes node_ids` array. Clicking it writes the current cluster's node-ID list verbatim into `IngesterConfig.node_ids`. Any node that joins later is *not* in that list, so the dispatcher never runs the ingester on the new node. The "All nodes" semantic needs to be a first-class field on the FSM, not a UI affordance over a frozen array.

## Smoking gun

[frontend/src/components/settings/NodeMultiSelect.tsx:42-50](frontend/src/components/settings/NodeMultiSelect.tsx#L42-L50):

```ts
const allSelected = sorted.every((n) => selected.has(n.id));
const toggleAll = () => {
  if (allSelected) {
    onChange([]);
  } else {
    onChange(sorted.map((n) => n.id));  // ← bakes current node-id snapshot
  }
};
```

`allSelected` is computed by "are all current nodes individually checked?" — so the checkbox state silently lies the moment the cluster scales up. `toggleAll` writes the current cluster snapshot, not an "all nodes" intent.

The proto, [backend/api/proto/gastrolog/v1/system.proto:321](backend/api/proto/gastrolog/v1/system.proto#L321), has `repeated bytes node_ids = 7;` with no `all_nodes: bool` flag and no special "empty = all" semantic.

## Repro

1. `just deploy kubernetes-up` (3 nodes: gastrolog-0/1/2)
2. Open Settings → Ingesters → any ingester → click "All nodes" → save
3. `just deploy kubernetes-expand 2` (cluster now 5 nodes: gastrolog-0..4)
4. Inspect the ingester. It runs on the original three only; gastrolog-3 and gastrolog-4 are not running it despite "All nodes" being "selected" in the UI.

## Fix

1. **Proto**: add `bool all_nodes = 9` to `IngesterConfig`. Regenerate.
2. **Dispatcher**: when `cfg.AllNodes`, target every cluster node on every tick / config-change / membership-change event; ignore `node_ids`. Critically, *resolve the node set every time*, not once at config-write — that's the whole point of the flag.
3. **NodeMultiSelect.tsx**: write `all_nodes=true, node_ids=[]` when "All nodes" is clicked; read back as "All nodes" checked when `all_nodes==true`. Disable / hide the individual checkboxes when "All nodes" is on (they're meaningless then). Update CLI `config ingester create/update` to accept an `--all-nodes` flag with the same semantic.
4. **Audit other config entities for the same trap.** Same "frozen-snapshot at config-time" pattern likely lurks elsewhere — vault placement / replica node lists, route fanout (if it has node targeting), scheduled jobs. Grep the FSM for any `repeated bytes <thing>_node_ids` or `repeated NodeAssignment` fields and audit each: does the consumer treat the list as a literal pin, or does it have a notion of "all nodes including future joiners"? Each one that lacks the latter is the same bug.

## Related

- Tied to gastrolog-1ex3b (cloud-vault config-update propagation) — both reflect "FSM holds a snapshot, runtime doesn't react to membership change".
- The deploy-recipe inline fix for `add-storage.sh` on `kubernetes-expand` / `swarm-expand` is a band-aid for storage but doesn't help ingester-on-all-nodes — that fix needs to live in the FSM, not in deploy automation.

When an ingester has `all_nodes: true`, the node inspector should show it under every node. Instead, it only appears under the node listed in the (legacy) `node_ids` field — typically the node where the ingester was originally created before `all_nodes` was toggled on.

**Root cause**: `frontend/src/components/inspector/NodeDetailPane.tsx:57` filters ingesters per node without consulting `allNodes`:

```ts
const ingesters = (allIngesters ?? []).filter(
  (i) => i.nodeIds.length === 0 || i.nodeIds.some((n) => encode(n) === nodeId),
);
```

Same class as gastrolog-my66y (cold-start dispatch ignored AllNodes). `IngesterCard`'s eligibility-count heuristic correctly guards with `!ingester.allNodes` at IngesterCard.tsx:42 — the node-detail filter is the only remaining stale read site.

**Fix**: mirror the backend's `shouldRunIngester` semantics in the frontend filter:

```ts
const ingesters = (allIngesters ?? []).filter(
  (i) => i.allNodes || i.nodeIds.length === 0 || i.nodeIds.some((n) => encode(n) === nodeId),
);
```

**Observable symptom**: cluster with `chatterbox` configured as all-nodes shows the ingester only on the original creator node's inspector pane; the other 3 nodes report 'No ingesters on this node' even though the ingester is actually running on all of them (verified via per-node CLI `config ingester status` after gastrolog-my66y's cold-start fix).

